# Meridian National Bank — IdentityIQ Lessons

Progressive, hands-on path to learn **SailPoint IdentityIQ 8.5** by implementing realistic IAM work for a fictitious bank.

**Company:** Meridian National Bank (MNB)  
**Your role:** IAM Engineer on the Identity Governance team  
**Platform:** Local IdentityIQ 8.5 lab from this repo

---

## Before you start

1. Complete [LOCAL_SETUP.md](../LOCAL_SETUP.md) until you can log in as `spadmin`.  
2. Read [INFRASTRUCTURE.md](../INFRASTRUCTURE.md) once for vocabulary.  
3. Copy lab files:

```bash
mkdir -p ~/iiq-lab-data
cp HRApplications.txt EmployeeData.txt ~/iiq-lab-data/
```

(Run the `cp` from this repo’s root.)

---

## Learning path

| # | Lesson | Skill focus | Time (approx.) |
| ---: | --- | --- | ---: |
| 01 | [Bank briefing & UI orientation](01-bank-briefing-and-ui.md) | Navigation, mental model | 45–60 min |
| 02 | [Authoritative HR source](02-authoritative-hr-source.md) | Delimited File app, aggregation | 60–90 min |
| 03 | [Build identity cubes](03-identity-cubes-and-refresh.md) | Correlation basics, Identity Refresh | 60 min |
| 04 | [Onboard bank applications](04-onboard-bank-applications.md) | Target apps, entitlements | 90 min |
| 05 | [Account correlation mastery](05-account-correlation.md) | Matching accounts → people | 60–90 min |
| 06 | [Birthright roles for bankers](06-birthright-roles.md) | Role model, assignment | 90 min |
| 07 | [Joiner / Mover / Leaver](07-joiner-mover-leaver.md) | Lifecycle events | 90–120 min |
| 08 | [Access requests & approvals](08-access-requests-approvals.md) | LCM request flow | 90 min |
| 09 | [SoD policies for banking](09-sod-policies.md) | Policy violations | 60–90 min |
| 10 | [Manager access certifications](10-access-certifications.md) | Campaigns, work items, email | 90–120 min |
| 11 | [Provisioning & troubleshooting](11-provisioning-and-troubleshooting.md) | Plans, tasks, debug habits | 90 min |
| 12 | [Audit-ready reporting & ops](12-reporting-and-ops.md) | Reports, hygiene, next steps | 60–90 min |

Work **in order**. Later lessons assume objects and data from earlier ones.

---

## How each lesson is structured

Every lesson file uses the same shape:

- **Story** — why Meridian Bank cares  
- **How it works** — concept in plain language  
- **Lesson goals** — what “done” means  
- **Tasks** — click-by-click / command steps  
- **Tips & tricks** — time-savers and gotchas  
- **Checkpoint** — self-test before continuing  
- **Stretch** — optional harder practice

---

## Meridian National Bank — quick lore

MNB is a mid-size retail + commercial bank. Regulators expect clean joiner/mover/leaver controls, SoD on payment functions, and periodic access reviews.

| Org signal | In the lab data |
| --- | --- |
| Employees & managers | `HRApplications.txt` (`managerId`, `departmentCode`, `status`) |
| IT system access | `EmployeeData.txt` (`itAccess` like `ODS`, `AWS`, `SAP`, `ELDAP`) |
| Certification mail | `email.txt` (example manager notifications) |

Suggested business mapping for `itAccess` codes (use consistently in lessons):

| Code | Bank meaning (fictitious) |
| --- | --- |
| `ELDAP` | Enterprise directory / login backbone |
| `ODS` | Operational Data Store (analytics) |
| `IBSI` | Internet Banking Support Interface |
| `Ecom` | E-commerce / digital channel ops |
| `SalesForce` | CRM for relationship managers |
| `AS500` | Legacy core / midrange operations access |
| `SAP` | Finance / ERP |
| `AWS` | Cloud admin / platform access |
| `DWRP` | Developer workstation / repo platform |

---

## Suggested weekly pace

- **Week 1:** Lessons 01–04  
- **Week 2:** Lessons 05–08  
- **Week 3:** Lessons 09–12 + stretch goals  

